# pytest.ini is the CANONICAL backend test config and MUST be committed:
# it sets DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE and the `testpaths` that make `pytest`
# discover both tests/ and servers/**/tests/. It was previously ignored,
# which is why CI had to hardcode `pytest tests/` and inline its env vars.
# Note pytest.ini outranks pyproject.toml/setup.cfg, so an ignored local
# copy would silently override CI.
